  "assumptions": [
    "Simplified simulation: no air resistance, and the ball starts at ground level on flat ground.",
    "Gravity is 9.8 m/s² straight down; the ball keeps its sideways speed and only its vertical speed changes.",
    "Each point is computed exactly from the projectile formulas, so the landing distance equals speed² × sin(2 × angle) ÷ 9.8. The ball is a point (drawn as a sphere), and the flight ends when it returns to ground height.",
    "A hit is a landing within 1.5 m of the target centre, both edges counted. Targets come in a fixed order (30 m, 45 m, 18 m); Reset clears score and trails and starts the same challenge.",
    "Every flight is shown over 2 seconds whatever its real duration, so screen time does not match the flight-time readout. Real balls slowed by air land shorter than shown."
  ],
  "program_note": null
}